ality is shown on the number line below.\n\n![](images/51/5127629c09f32bb8ed7872b476322d6973e44e82be7977492c8dd0967d3cb0ec.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $2x \\leq -2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x & \\le -2 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\le \\frac{-2}{2} \\\\ x & \\le -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe solution to this inequality is shown on the number line below.\n\n![](images/35/35e30bc9c45b08793d847c8750698f7d9dab781438405239ed4483ce82f2dcfb.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](images/fe/fe4c223767cb06d9d620d32f5e668c7305688b3870bf0317304c56b11053e19f.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $\\color{blue}-3 \\leq x \\leq -1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065437 #edb/ref 1065 8687 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065437 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "79460753-2a4c-5227-8dcd-7355a1841558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065437 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048267 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069131 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186511567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186511580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1039 "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Less Than (or Equal To) Symbol" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068491 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068717 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "e107f878-5b22-54bf-90fc-b8ea8a22c77d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069132 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069133 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186511521 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186566222 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186566252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1039 "Cases Where the Coefficient in the Absolute Value Is Negative" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068718 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "65964b91-8f0e-5ffc-97d3-e5b87a6bade5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050680 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069134 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186069290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186511463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186511490 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186511573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186566272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1039 "Absolute Value Inequalities Containing a Greater Than (or Equal To) Symbol" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068719 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c4f7e042-a8fa-50c8-a502-1397138dc380" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1045 "Absolute Value Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069604 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1050 780.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068978 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "1e92c4a4-e0ad-5ee8-8851-82d431bca7f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069604 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069604 #edb/ref 1061 145541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069604 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e46e2f60-2005-54d4-8f5c-97b81542dd48" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069604 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070026 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069605 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069605 #edb/ref 1061 145542 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069605 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "461b27d5-3e08-5e71-9e57-464e06a7b559" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069605 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068717 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069606 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069606 #edb/ref 1061 145546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069606 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95df2774-fa6c-5c44-85c3-1203c060ec1a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069606 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068718 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069607 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069607 #edb/ref 1061 145550 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069607 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3706f0b6-4695-54b2-974b-2b4f77638739" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069607 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186070027 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069608 #edb/ref 1061 145551 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "419f8ba9-27c0-5918-8ecd-eff659df7bb5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070026 #edb/ref 1064 "**Absolute value inequalities** combine two basic concepts: absolute value and inequality. The absolute value of a number is its distance from zero, while an inequality specifies a range of values.\n\nConsider a simple absolute value inequality, as follows:\n\n$$\n|x| < 7\n$$\n\nThis inequality specifies every number $x$ that is less than a distance of $7$ from $0$. So, it represents the same thing as the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-7 < x < 7\n$$\n\nTo solve an absolute value inequality, we first convert it to a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. Then, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods.\n\nTo illustrate, let's solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n|2x+3| \\leq 5\n$$\n\nFirst, we interpret the inequality: the inequality specifies every number $2x+3$ whose distance from zero is less than or equal to $5.$ So, it represents the same thing as the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n-5 \\leq 2x+3 \\leq 5\n$$\n\nNow, we can solve the compound inequality using the usual methods:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5\\le 2x+3\\le 5 \\\\ -8\\le 2x\\le 2 \\\\ -4\\le x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070026 #edb/ref 1065 8825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070026 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "53ecd5cc-486a-584d-abc8-f75ec26f12cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070026 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070027 #edb/ref 1064 "We take a similar approach for absolute value inequalities involving the \"greater than\" symbol. To illustrate, consider the following absolute value inequality:\n\n$$\n|x| \\geq 6\n$$\n\nTo solve this absolute value inequality, we convert it into a compound inequality to remove the absolute value. The inequality specifies every number $x$ whose distance from zero is greater than or equal to $6.$ This corresponds to the following compound inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & \\le -6 & \\text{or} &  & x & \\ge 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use the word \"or\" instead of \"and\" since only one of the inequalities $x\\leq-6$ or $x\\geq 6$ needs to be true for $|x| \\geq 6$ to be true." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070027 #edb/ref 1065 8830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070027 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "93e8452a-53ea-5e58-807a-00e95af99af1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186070027 #edb/ref 1067 "Greater Than (or Equal To) Absolute Value Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186095935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186095936 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186095937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186095938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095934 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186095939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095934 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095934 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095934 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "65c0f080-99fe-57f2-a719-d49f2825bb86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095935 #edb/ref 1080 "images/eb/eb42f18a8d83b77a18b8e796c55cb834b4288bebfd028bd89bfe58bda39252af.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095935 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095935 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a2e99f4a-91f0-5666-986c-d96a19fd2379" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095936 #edb/ref 1080 "images/24/24cf5282bb402e4c3a3320fdfbf37e6c866692e8c646d558738c289a999d3a36.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095936 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095936 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a610a33f-18cd-5e82-8634-239c2bde6252" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095937 #edb/ref 1080 "images/a9/a91fc49b59add56f76c2eab2def379db811cc7787ee3f809e0cb3f7c70d838df.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095937 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095937 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dee44144-6f77-53e4-9c87-f3521ff5b169" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186095938 #edb/ref 1080 "images